    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` passes: birthDate `1990-01-01` against the default registrationDate (today, 2026-09-08) yields 36 years \u2192 `ADULT`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented owner age-band derivation across the standard Spring layers:\n\n**Spec** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added `birthDate` (optional, ISO `date`) to `OwnerFields` \u2014 the request input.\n- Added `ageBand` (readOnly enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the derived `Owner` schema. These regenerate the DTOs on build.\n\n**Domain** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n- Added a derived `@Transient getAgeBand()` that computes whole years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` via `Period`, mapping to `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when either date is absent \u2014 the single definition of the rule, alongside the existing `getRegion()`/`getMembershipNumber()` derived values.\n\n**Mapping** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)\n- `birthDate` auto-maps by name both directions.\n- Added an `ageBand(owner)` expression mapping that renders the model's string band into the generated `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` (null when not derivable), following the existing `locality`/`contactPreference` pattern.\n\n**Persistence** (schema.sql for hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres)\n- Added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the value round-trips through create \u2192 read.\n\nThe band is computed against `registrationDate` as specified \u2014 and since `registrationDate` defaults to the server date (rolled to a business day) when omitted, an owner submitted with only a `birthDate` still gets a band.",
